// CLAIM: Cryptography: some built, most deliberately not
// HOLDS: absent
// TERMS: aes, chacha, ed25519, x25519, argon2, bcrypt, scrypt
// WHY: these are BOUND, never written here — no control over instruction timing, and the
//      curves need arbitrary-precision integers the language does not have. A hand-rolled one
//      appearing in `lib/` is the failure this whole section exists to prevent, and it would
//      look perfectly fine while being wrong.

